---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p>KoAkademy uses a documentation workflow with two source types:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code> is the only remaining root-level canonical Markdown source; it syncs to <code>docs/src/content/docs/start-here/contributing.mdx</code>.</li>\n<li>The other foundational guides (installation, deployment, configuration, troubleshooting, development, architecture, FAQ) and all specialized guides (System Internals, Maintainers, User Guides, Enrollment Blueprints, API Reference, OSS) are <strong>native MDX files</strong> authored directly under <code>docs/src/content/docs/</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Architecture &amp; Sync Pipeline</h2>\n<pre><code>Canonical Root Docs (e.g. CONTRIBUTING.md)\n   │\n   ├──▶ npm run docs:sync (scripts/sync-docs.mjs)\n   │       └── Generates MDX mirrors with frontmatter &amp; warning headers\n   │\n   └──▶ npm run docs:check (scripts/check-docs.mjs)\n           ├── Validates mirrors are up to date\n           ├── Checks that internal links resolve correctly\n           └── Verifies API contract documentation\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Mapping of Canonical Files to Generated Mirrors</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Canonical Root File</th>\n<th>Generated Site Mirror</th>\n<th>Sidebar Placement</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code></td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/start-here/contributing.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Start Here → Contributing</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The installation, deployment, configuration, troubleshooting, development, architecture, and FAQ pages are native MDX files edited directly under <code>docs/src/content/docs/</code>.</p>\n<div class="doc-callout doc-callout-caution">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Never Edit Generated Mirrors Directly</p><p>Generated MDX mirror files contain a <code>{/* GENERATED FILE. Source: ... */}</code> header. Any manual edits to generated files will be overwritten by <code>npm run docs:sync</code> and will fail the CI check <code>npm run docs:check</code>. Always edit the root canonical Markdown file instead.</p>\n</div><h2>Decision Table: Where to Write New Documentation</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>If you are writing...</th>\n<th>Edit this location</th>\n<th>Workflow</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Setup, installation, or server deployment</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/self-hosting/*.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Environment variables or service config</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/self-hosting/configuration.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Contributor workflows, testing rules, setup</td>\n<td><code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code> or <code>docs/src/content/docs/start-here/development.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit root file or native MDX ➔ run <code>npm run docs:sync</code> for CONTRIBUTING</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>High-level runtime or architecture overview</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/start-here/architecture.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deep system internals (auth, frontend, queues)</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/system/*.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Module development or maintainer processes</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/maintainers/*.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>User and staff operational guides</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/user-guide/*.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Enrollment blueprint engine guides</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/enrollment-policies/*.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Public REST API reference</td>\n<td><code>docs/src/content/docs/api/*.mdx</code></td>\n<td>Edit native MDX directly</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Running Local Verification</h2>\n<p>Always run the full documentation verification before pushing:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-sh"># 1. Sync any canonical changes to their mirrors\nnpm run docs:sync\n\n# 2. Check for stale mirrors and broken internal links\nnpm run docs:check\n\n# 3. Test the Astro production build locally\nnpm --prefix docs run build\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Documentation Website Stack</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Framework:</strong> Astro 5 with <code>@astrojs/starlight</code> and <code>@astrojs/mdx</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Search:</strong> Built-in client-side Pagefind indexing.</li>\n<li><strong>Typography &amp; Styling:</strong> Self-hosted <code>@fontsource/inter</code> and <code>@fontsource/jetbrains-mono</code> with custom CSS matching the application&#39;s shadcn/ui palette (<code>docs/src/styles/custom.css</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Sidebar Navigation:</strong> Configured explicitly in <code>docs/astro.config.mjs</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>In-App Integration:</strong> The same generated documentation files are rendered inside the running application at <code>/docs</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Automated Deployment (GitHub Pages)</h2>\n<p>The documentation site is automatically built and deployed to GitHub Pages on documentation changes merged into <code>master</code> via <code>.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml</code>.</p>\n<p>When deploying:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Ensure GitHub Pages is configured with <strong>Source: GitHub Actions</strong> in repository settings.</li>\n<li>The site publishes to <code>https://yukazakiri.github.io/koakademy/</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation System"
  path="/docs/maintainers/documentation"
  description="Canonical Markdown, generated MDX mirrors, the validation contract, and how this site is built and deployed."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
